      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PERFECT JENNY (6) finds it hard to break through. Finished in the minors latest when third (25.92) at Shepparton and may be close to breaking through. Form from her last run is proving to be solid. Leading chance again. KUNAMA NAMADGI (4) comes off an average effort last start when seventh at this track over 500m behind Don't Tell Danni (29.23) in a Bottom Up - Grade 5. Cannot be underestimated. VESTA BALE (8) showed strong pace early from the inside rail and stuck on well despite missing the frame, finishing fourth over 450m Shepparton in 25.96. Some good form is emerging from her last run. Has the ability to give this a shake. MISS SOOKY (1) was in the money last start from this box and should feature again.",
